molqrc is dual-licensed, file by file. The SPDX expression for the project as a
whole is:

    MIT AND BSD-3-Clause

Both licences are permissive and impose only attribution requirements, so
redistributing molqrc means carrying both notices below.

## MIT — the QR Code engine

The engine in `src/` is derived from Project Nayuki's `qrcodegen` (Rust),
https://github.com/nayuki/QR-Code-generator. It remains under that library's
MIT licence, Copyright (c) Project Nayuki, and every engine file says so in its
header.

Full text: LICENSE-MIT

## BSD-3-Clause — everything else

The test suites (`src/tests.rs`, `tests/`), the WebAssembly bindings (`wasm/`), the web
demo (`molqrc_web/`), the verification tooling (`scripts/`, `examples/`) and the
documentation are original work, Copyright (c) 2024-2026 Roy Kid, licensed under
the BSD 3-Clause License.

Full text: LICENSE-BSD-3-CLAUSE

## Binary distributions

Compiled artifacts — the crates.io package, the `@molcrafts/molqrc-wasm` npm
package and the `.wasm` binaries — contain code under both licences, and are
therefore distributed under `MIT AND BSD-3-Clause`.
